# FakerAI

Defensive scam-baiting research tool. The person at the keyboard plays the scammer and both
UIs say so on screen; an AI decoy stays in persona,
baits for details, and files confirmed scammers into a local database. The analyst pane is
never mentioned by the decoy.

## Stack

- Two surfaces on one server: the analyst console at `/` (back office) and the dating app at
 `/tinder` (product). They must always link to each other in the UI — console header button
 “Open the dating app”, and the stage caption beside the phone links back to `/`.
- Both surfaces run the same pipeline and must show the same three stages. The console has a
 Match dropdown bound to the same deck, a pre-screen card, a phase card (owner → Faker
 takeover → blocked) and a case gate line. Picking a blocked profile there gets the same 403
 and disables the composer. `/?match=<id>` pairs with `/tinder?open=<id>`.
- Python FastAPI (`app/main.py`) + vanilla `static/` frontend, two tabs: Live chat and Case files. Palette: `#00C8CB` / `#00A3B0` accents on `#0B1020` navy, `#334155` lines, `#E2E8F0` text.
- Local host: `npm run dev` (`scripts/dev.js`) creates `.venv` if needed, installs `requirements.txt`, and starts uvicorn with reload on port 8787.
- Live chat talks to the live model as Ava Lin. Do not show a 1/2 mode switch. Do not show the word “demo” in the UI except as internal mode ids. Analyst score and the fraud-report ticks come from `/api/chat`. Score climbs with the lure and jumps when a bank account or wallet is given; that auto-files the case and plays the police/bank handover. The only decoy is Ava Lin.
- Tinder skin (`/tinder`) is the product demo: a 14-profile deck, then the chat. Profiles come from
 `app/profiles.py` (`GET /api/profiles`) and are screened on photo/bio/account facts only —
 blocked at risk ≥70 (chat never opens, `/api/session` returns 403), caution ≥30, else clear.
 Photos are SVGs generated by `scripts/make_photos.py` into `static/photos/`; `look` is the
 single source of truth, so copying a `look` really does reuse the face (p05 reuses p01).
 In the chat the person at the keyboard plays the match (left bubbles); the owner's account
 answers on the right. `/tinder?open=<id>` opens a thread directly, `?script=1` runs canned turns.
- Two chat phases. `phase: "user"` — the model writes the account owner's ordinary dating replies,
 no baiting. `phase: "takeover"` — Faker runs the account and baits. The switch happens the turn a
 money ask lands (`signals.MONEY_SIGNALS`, checked before the model call so the reply is already
 the decoy's) or when the model scores ≥65 as scammer. The UI shows `FAKER HAS TAKEN OVER THIS CHAT`.
- The case only closes once a bank account or wallet is on the record — a verdict alone is not a
 case. Until then the decoy keeps stalling and asking. `static/handover.js` owns the handover
 animation for both UIs.
- SQLite at `data/decoy.db` (`app/db.py`), gitignored — tables `cases`, `case_iocs`, `case_messages`
- Serve on port 8787 — port 8000 is blocked on this machine

## Model access

- `app/llm.py` owns the provider chain: Poe (`POE_API_KEY`) → DeepSeek → Ling (`LING_API_KEY`) → OpenRouter →
 any OpenAI-compatible (`LLM_BASE_URL`) → offline heuristics. Failed providers cool down
 for two minutes.
- Poe is OpenAI-compatible (`https://api.poe.com/v1`). Keys from https://poe.com/api/keys.
  Default bot `Claude-Haiku-4.5` (fast, cheap). Override with `POE_MODEL`. Chat Completions
  ignores `response_format`; the parser still extracts a JSON object from the reply.
- Ling is open-weight with no single official API — set `LING_BASE_URL` to match the host
  that issued the key (ZenMux default, or Novita/OpenRouter). All three are reachable here.
  `scripts/check_key.py` probes a key against every candidate host to identify its owner.
- The current key is an OpenRouter free-tier key, so `LING_BASE_URL` points at OpenRouter.
 Free capacity returns 429 under load — `llm.py` retries twice with backoff, then falls
 through to the next model (`ling-3.0-flash-fin:free`, `glm-5.2:free`, `minimax-m3:free`).
- Current DeepSeek IDs are `deepseek-v4-flash` / `deepseek-v4-pro`; `deepseek-chat` was retired.
  V4 thinks by default, so `DEEPSEEK_THINKING=disabled` keeps chat latency sane.
- `api.deepseek.com` is SNI-filtered on this machine (TLS reset, TCP fine). That is a network
  fact, not a bug — add `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` or use a VPN, do not "fix" the code.
- When no provider answers, `/api/chat` returns 503 and the decoy stays silent; the UI shows a
  red banner and restores the typed message. Never fake an in-character reply.
  `DECOY_ALLOW_FALLBACK=1` opts back into the canned offline heuristics.
- `POST /api/providers/reload` re-reads `.env` so a pasted key works without a restart.
- Keys live in `.env`, never committed.

## Behaviour

- One model call per turn returns the in-character reply, the verdict, and the intel object
  (`app/agent.py`). `app/fallback.py` runs when no provider answers and the UI labels it `local-fallback`.
- One persona: `dating` (Ava Lin). Sessions lock to her immediately. Live chat always uses the live model. Canned dating turns only run on `/tinder?script=1`.
- Reply in the user's language. Benign chats wrap up after ≥3 turns and go quiet.
- Intel accumulates across turns in `app/intel.py` (identity / contact / payment /
  infrastructure / playbook), model output merged with a regex safety net.
- Cases file automatically at score ≥ `DECOY_AUTO_RECORD_SCORE`, confidence ≥
  `DECOY_AUTO_RECORD_CONFIDENCE` **and** a payment rail in the intel, or manually via
  **Flag as swindler**. Upsert per session. Benign sessions are never stored.
- Any move at the user's money counts as a scam, whatever the wrapper: loan, top-up, gift card,
  clearance / unfreeze fee, investment platform, or receiving money through their account.
- Repeated values across cases surface as "shared infrastructure".

## Conventions

- Regex cues in `app/signals.py` are analyst hints only — do not trust them as the verdict
- Dedupe IOCs with `intel.dedupe_key`, which ignores spacing on accounts, phones and
 wallets so the model and the regex net cannot file the same account twice
- Decoy never sends money, OTPs, seed phrases, or ID, but should actively draw out
  their account, wallet, link, and handle — that is what the case file is made of
- Do not add WhatsApp/Telegram/bank-freeze routing unless asked; this phase is local only
- `scripts/smoke_test.py` and `scripts/api_check.py` verify the pipeline without a browser
